provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: In the watchlist, show movies I haven't watched yet before the ones I've watched.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist  (The request is a display-order concern isolated to the watchlist view. The store's items order is part of existing behaviour (insertion order, shared with other consumers), so the sort belongs in the watchlist component's existing `movies` signal. No interface change is needed since `movies` already exposes `Signal<WatchItem[]>`; only its derived order changes. An acceptance test pins the new stable unwatched-first ordering and its reactivity.)
round 1: owners watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (The ordering change itself is correct: tsc is clean and both governor acceptance tests (unwatched-before-watched, including reactive re-ordering on toggleWatched) pass. The only failures are two watchlist unit tests, both asserting "false to be true" right after a DOM toggle. I cannot see those tests, so the owner must first rule out a genuine regression in per-row DOM wiring (ids vs loop indices, double-toggle via row bubbling) introduced while implementing the sort; if the wiring is verifiably correct, the failures are positional assertions pinning the old insertion order, which the user's request intentionally changes — in that case the owner must route a test-change request to me rather than editing the tests.)
round 2: owners watchlist=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 3: plan -> watchlist  (The two failing tests pin the old insertion order by asserting list position ("first rendered checkbox is checked after clicking the first item"). The user's request intentionally re-orders unwatched before watched, so that positional assertion can no longer hold; the owner verified the component wiring is defect-free and proposed minimal, intent-preserving updates that keep the real DOM interactions and assert the clicked movie's watched state by stable identity. I approve exactly those two test changes and re-instruct the watchlist owner; no other unit is implicated.)
round 3: owners watchlist=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 4: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc clean, 33 tests passing) and the watchlist now lists unwatched movies before watched ones, with reactive re-ordering on toggle confirmed by the acceptance tests.)

