        "reason": "Step 1 verification (no component/template defect): onRowClick($event, movie.id) receives the clicked row's own id and toggles only that row's movie; clicking a row's blank space toggles once (target is the li or a non-interactive child, so the closest('a, button, input') guard does not bail). Verified with a new test using unwatched ids 10/20/30: a blank-space click on the LAST rendered row marks only Movie 30 watched and leaves Movies 10/20 untouched. The failure is purely positional: after items()[0].click() toggles Movie 1 to watched, Movie 1 re-orders behind the still-unwatched Movie 2 ([Movie 2, Movie 1]), so the old assertion `checkbox().checked` - which re-queries the first rendered row - read Movie 2's unchecked checkbox ('expected false to be true'). Requested minimal, intent-preserving update: keep the identical blank-space DOM click on the first row and keep asserting that the clicked movie becomes watched, but identify that movie by its stable title (checkboxFor('Movie 1')) rather than by list position. Same assertion strength, position-independent.",
